course: dictionary
lesson: 7517
title: Powder: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Powder» can be a thing or an action, so the sentence tells you which. As a noun it is a dry substance made of very tiny pieces. «Add a spoon of cocoa powder to the milk.» Cocoa powder is something you add, so powder here is a thing.
explain: As a verb, powder means to put powder on something. «She powdered the cake with sugar.» The sugar is the powder, and she put it on the cake. Ask yourself: is the word naming something, or is someone doing something?
explain: Context also gives safety clues. «Unknown powders must never be tasted or sniffed.» Washing powder is poisonous, so a powder in a cupboard without a clear label is not a snack. When you are not sure what a powder is, leave it alone and ask an adult.
fact: A powder is a dry substance made of very tiny pieces, like flour, dust or crushed chalk.
fact: Examples of powders you may use are «baking powder», «cocoa powder» and «baby powder».
fact: Powders can be poured like liquids, but they are still solids.
fact: «Powder» can also mean fresh, light, dry snow, which is a favourite word for skiers.
fact: Never taste or sniff an unknown powder, because «washing powder» is poisonous.
exercise: «A firework's bang comes from powder burning so fast inside a closed case that the hot gas bursts it.» What makes the bang? | Wet sand pressed into a tube | Hot gas cooling down slowly | *Powder burning very fast inside a closed case | A loud band playing nearby
exercise: What should you never do with a powder you do not know? | *Taste it or sniff it | Read the label on the tub | Ask an adult what it is | Put it in a sealed box
exercise: «She powdered the cake with sugar.» What does powdered mean here? | Cut something into slices | Wash something with water | Take something away | *Put powder on something
test: Which of these is a powder? | A wooden spoon | A cup of warm tea | A glass of milk | *Cocoa powder
test: Fresh, light, dry snow that skiers love is called what? | Sleet | *Powder | Ice | Slush
exam: Sam finds a tub of unknown white powder in the cupboard; what is the safest thing to do? | Sniff it to check if it smells of sugar | Taste a little to find out what it is | Sprinkle it on his toast to see | *Leave it alone and tell an adult
